  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:business-taxonomy skos:definition "The business taxonomy categorizes and organizes data content that is to be used in the organization's Data Marketplace to enable a more intuitive user experience for browse & discovery."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:filters skos:definition "Used for evaluating a dataset against predetermined rules, conditions, or business logic to selectively include, exclude, or partition records or attributes for downstream processing, analysis, storage, or access."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:business-partner skos:definition "Business Partner domain is defined as the concepts related to organizations conducting business with the organization. Includes concepts such as account, bill, interaction, problem, revenue & settlement and statistics."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer skos:definition "Customer domain is defined by concepts relating to the individual or organization that has purchased products or services from the organization. Includes concepts such as billing, interactions, problems and statistics."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:enterprise skos:definition "Enterprise domain is defined as concepts related to the day-to-day business operations of the organization, including its people, finance, real estate, supply chain, information technology."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:market-and-sales skos:definition "Market & Sales domain is defined as concepts such as competitor, concept, sales statistics, sales channels, sales commissions, sales leads and marketing campaigns."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:patterns skos:definition "The Pattern Domain is defined as containing abstract aggregate business entities that are not directly usable and must be sub-classed to be used."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product skos:definition "Product domain is defined as concepts relating the physical items sold by the organization. Includes concepts such as offering, configuration, order, performance, usage, pricing and loyalty."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:resource skos:definition "Resource domain is defined as the concepts related to physical or logical items that support the services sold by the organization. Includes concepts such as capacity, configuration, order, performance, specification, test, topology and trouble."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service skos:definition "Service domain is defined as the concepts related to intangible offerings sold by the organization, such as wireless, home internet, the organization, FWA. Includes concepts such as configuration, order, performance, plan, usage and problems."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:shared skos:definition "The Shared Domain is defined as concepts that are directly usable (without any specificity) by several Domains."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner-account skos:definition "Represents a business partner within a company’s systems, containing relevant information and interactions."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner-contract-management skos:definition "Managing the lifecycle of contracts with business partners, including renewals and amendments."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner-ecosystem-management skos:definition "The strategic oversight and coordination of a network of interconnected partners, fostering collaboration and value creation."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner-integration-process skos:definition "The steps involved in onboarding and integrating a new partner into a company’s systems and processes."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner-performance skos:definition "Evaluation of a partner’s effectiveness and contribution to shared goals."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner-role skos:definition "Defines the specific function and responsibilities of a business partner within the collaboration."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:account-hierarchy skos:definition "A structured representation of partner relationships, reflecting parent-child or subsidiary connections."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:account-segmentation skos:definition "Categorizing partner accounts based on specific criteria, such as revenue, industry, or partnership type."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:contact-role skos:definition "Defines the specific function and responsibilities of an individual contact within a partner organization."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-agreement skos:definition "A formal document outlining the terms and conditions of service delivery between a company and its partner."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner-market-share skos:definition "The percentage of a specific market controlled or influenced by a particular partner."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:dealer skos:definition "An independent entity authorized to sell and distribute a company’s products to end customers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:partner skos:definition "A general term encompassing various types of collaborative relationships, including resellers, distributors and technology providers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:retailer skos:definition "A business that sells goods directly to consumers through physical stores or online channels."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-provider skos:definition "A company that delivers services, such as telecommunications, IT support, or consulting, to businesses or individuals."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:supplier skos:definition "Similar to a vendor, but often implies a longer-term relationship and a focus on raw materials or components."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:vendor skos:definition "An entity that supplies goods or services to another business, typically as part of a supply chain."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-account-management skos:definition "Managing customer accounts, including account creation, profile updates and account closures."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-acquisition-and-conversion skos:definition
      "Attracting new customers and converting them into paying customers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-behavioral-data skos:definition "Information collected about customer actions and interactions, such as website browsing history, purchase history and app usage."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-care-and-call-center skos:definition "Providing support and assistance to customers through phone calls, emails and other channels."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-churn skos:definition "The rate at which customers stop doing business with a company."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-feedback skos:definition "Information provided by customers about their experiences with a company’s products, services, or brand."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-interaction-and-engagement skos:definition
      "Activities and communications that foster relationships and encourage ongoing interaction with customers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-journey skos:definition "The complete experience a customer has with a company, from initial awareness to post-purchase interactions."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-profile skos:definition "Defines the Customer Profile type information"@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-referral skos:definition "A recommendation from a satisfied customer that encourages others to engage with a company."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-retention-and-growth skos:definition "Strategies and initiatives focused on retaining existing customers and encouraging repeat business."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-support skos:definition "A specific method or platform used to provide customer support, such as phone, email, live chat, or social media which typically aligns with the Partner Support Organization channels."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-account-activations skos:definition "Activating new customer accounts and services."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-account-cancellations skos:definition "Processing customer requests to cancel accounts or services."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-account-closure-and-retention skos:definition
      "Managing the process of closing customer accounts, including handling outstanding balances and attempting to retain customers if possible."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-account-creation-and-onboarding skos:definition
      "The process of creating new customer accounts and guiding customers through the initial setup and onboarding process."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-profile-management skos:definition "Maintaining accurate and up-to-date customer profiles, including contact information, preferences and purchase history."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-subscriptions-and-entitlements skos:definition
      "Managing customer subscriptions to services and ensuring customers have access to the appropriate features and benefits."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-acquisition-cost skos:definition "The average expense incurred to acquire a new customer."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-conversion skos:definition "The process of turning a potential customer into a paying customer."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-experience skos:definition "Evaluating and optimizing the overall experience customers have when interacting with a company through all service channels & touchpoints."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-plan-recommendations-and-changes skos:definition
      "The process of analyzing a customer’s current service plan and usage patterns to recommend more suitable or cost-effective plans, and then implementing any desired changes."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-product-and-feature-usage skos:definition
      "Understanding how customers use your products or services, including frequency, features used and pain points."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-usage skos:definition "Understanding how customers use your products or services, including frequency, features used and pain points over time, which is used for rating, billing, usage analytics, and customer profiling."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:digital-experience skos:definition "Evaluating and optimizing the overall experience customers have when interacting with a company through digital channels."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:contact-center-performance skos:definition "Measuring the effectiveness and efficiency of the call center in handling customer interactions."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-call skos:definition "Incoming and outgoing phone calls from customers seeking assistance or information."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-contact skos:definition "Any interaction between a customer and a company, regardless of the channel used."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-incident skos:definition "A reported issue or problem experienced by a customer."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-issue skos:definition "A specific problem or challenge faced by a customer."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-request skos:definition "A specific ask or inquiry from a customer."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:agent-availability skos:definition "Ensuring sufficient staffing levels to handle incoming customer contacts promptly."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:agent-performance skos:definition "Evaluating the performance of individual agents based on metrics such as call resolution rate, customer satisfaction and adherence to procedures."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:agent-productivity skos:definition "Measuring the output and efficiency of individual call center agents."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:average-handling-time skos:definition "The average duration of a customer interaction with a call center agent."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:conversation-handling skos:definition "Analyzing the flow and effectiveness of conversations between agents and customers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-case-resolution skos:definition "Tracking the timeliness and effectiveness of resolving customer issues."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:messaging-performance skos:definition "Evaluating the effectiveness of messaging channels, such as live chat and email, in handling customer interactions."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:overall-performance skos:definition "Assessing the overall effectiveness of the contact center in meeting customer needs and business objectives."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:sentiment-guidance skos:definition "Using technology to analyze customer sentiment during interactions and provide guidance to agents."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-case-resolution-time-and-efficiency skos:definition
      "Measures of how effectively resources are used to resolve customer cases, often considering factors like resolution time, first contact resolution rate, and customer satisfaction."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-case-volume-and-handling skos:definition "The total number of customer cases (issues, complaints, requests) received within a specific timeframe and the processes and procedures used to manage and resolve customer cases efficiently and effectively."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:call-in-rates skos:definition "Tracking the volume of incoming calls to the call center."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:call-routing-and-queuing skos:definition "Directing customer calls to the appropriate agents or departments and managing call queues."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:call-volume skos:definition "The total number of calls received by a call center or customer service department within a specific timeframe."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:first-call-resolution skos:definition "Resolving customer issues on the first contact to improve customer satisfaction."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:interaction-frequency-and-duration skos:definition
      "Analyzing the frequency and length of customer interactions to identify patterns and areas for improvement."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:case-breakdown skos:definition "Categorizing and analyzing customer incidents to identify common issues and trends."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-problem skos:definition "A general term for any issue a customer may encounter."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-problem-report skos:definition "A formal record of a customer issue, including details about the problem and any steps taken to resolve it."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-trouble-ticket skos:definition "A digital or physical record created to document and track a customer’s reported issue or service request until it is resolved."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:churn-prediction skos:definition "Identifying customers at risk of churning"@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:churn-prevention skos:definition "Developing strategies to retain customers at risk of churning."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:model-scoring skos:definition "Evaluating the accuracy and effectiveness of predictive models, including scores, churn propensities, purchasing propensities and product recommendations used for further analytical reporting"@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-complaints skos:definition "Expressions of dissatisfaction and related troubleshooting from customers regarding a product, service, or interaction."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-effort-score skos:definition "Assessing how easy it is for customers to interact with your business."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-feature-feedback skos:definition "Input from customers regarding desired product features or improvements."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-survey skos:definition "A structured questionnaire used to gather quantitative and qualitative feedback from customers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-after-call-survey skos:definition "A short survey presented to customers after a call with customer service, typically used to gauge customer satisfaction and identify areas for improvement."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-activity skos:definition "Activity that pertains to a specific customer"@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-support-interactions skos:definition "Analyzing interactions between customers and support agents to identify trends and areas for improvement."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-to-customer-interactions skos:definition "Facilitating and encouraging communication and collaboration among customers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:digital-interactions skos:definition "Engaging with customers through digital channels, such as email, chatbots and mobile apps."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:online-reviews skos:definition "Monitoring and responding to customer reviews posted on websites and platforms."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:sales-interactions skos:definition "Managing interactions between sales representatives and customers throughout the sales process."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:social-media-monitoring skos:definition "Tracking brand mentions and conversations about a company on social media platforms."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:authentication skos:definition "Verifying a customer’s identity to grant access to accounts or services."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-journey-completion skos:definition "Successfully guiding a customer through their desired interaction or transaction."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-journey-resolution skos:definition "Addressing and resolving any issues or challenges a customer encounters during their journey."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-touchpoints skos:definition "Specific interactions a customer has the organization facing processes either digitally or external communications or internal interactions."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-profile-demographics skos:definition "Basic characteristics of a customer, such as age, gender, location and socioeconomic status."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-profile-personalization skos:definition "Using customer data to create customized experiences and communications."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-profile-segmentation skos:definition "Dividing customers into groups based on shared characteristics to tailor marketing and service efforts."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-testimonial skos:definition "A positive statement from a customer about their experience with a company’s products or services."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:influencer-marketing skos:definition "Partnering with individuals with a strong online presence to promote products or services to their followers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:referral-program-data skos:definition "Tracking and analyzing the effectiveness of customer referral programs."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-centricity skos:definition "A business approach that prioritizes customer needs and experiences in all aspects of operations. Includes the organization's Rewards"@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-lifetime-value skos:definition "The predicted total revenue a customer will generate for a company over their entire relationship."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-satisfaction skos:definition "Meeting or exceeding customer expectations for products, services and interactions."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-trust-and-perception skos:definition "Building and maintaining a positive brand image and reputation among customers."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-value-optimization skos:definition "Maximizing the value a company delivers to its customers throughout their relationship."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:loyalty-program-and-rewards skos:definition "Offering incentives and rewards to encourage customer loyalty and repeat purchases."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:billing-and-payment-support skos:definition "Addressing customer inquiries and resolving issues related to billing, payments and account balances."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:live-chat-support skos:definition "Offering real-time support to customers through a chat interface on a website or app."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:sales-support skos:definition "Assisting customers with product information, pricing and the purchasing process."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:self-service-support skos:definition "Providing customers with resources and tools to resolve issues on their own, such as knowledge bases, FAQs and online forums."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:social-media-support skos:definition "Responding to customer inquiries and resolving issues through social media platforms."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:technical-support skos:definition "Providing assistance with technical issues related to products or services through multiple channels."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:financial-management skos:definition "The planning, organizing, directing and controlling of the financial activities of an enterprise to achieve its objectives."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:human-resources-management skos:definition "The strategic approach to managing an organization’s most valued assets: its people."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:legal skos:definition "The framework of rules and regulations that govern the conduct of businesses and individuals."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:operations-management skos:definition "The administration of business practices to create the highest level of efficiency possible within an organization."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:expenses-and-cost-management skos:definition "The processes and strategies used to control and reduce expenses incurred by an enterprise."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:financial-statements skos:definition "Formal records that provide an overview of the organization's financial position and performance."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:profitability skos:definition "The ability of the organization to generate profit."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:revenue-and-revenue-management skos:definition "The processes and strategies used to generate and maximize revenue for an enterprise."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:treasury-and-financing skos:definition "The management of the organization's financial resources, including cash, debt and equity."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:capital-expenditures skos:definition "Investments in long-term assets, such as property, plant and equipment."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:cost skos:definition "An expenditure incurred by an enterprise in the course of its operations."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:operating-expense skos:definition "Expenses incurred in the normal course of business operations."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:allocations-and-charges skos:definition "The assignment of indirect costs to specific cost objects."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:cost-of-goods-sold skos:definition "The direct costs associated with producing goods sold by an enterprise."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:gains-and-losses skos:definition "Increases or decreases in the value of assets or liabilities."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:losses-and-write-offs skos:definition "Expenses recognized when assets lose value or become unusable."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:commissions skos:definition "Payments made to employees based on performance, including direct commissions, CCRS and Spiff."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:compensation-and-benefits skos:definition "Costs associated with employee salaries, wages and benefits."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:information-technology-and-technology skos:definition
      "Expenses related to information technology systems and services, such as software, hardware, IT support."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:marketing-and-advertising skos:definition "Costs incurred to promote products or services."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:occupancy-and-utilities skos:definition "Costs associated with occupying and maintaining business facilities, such as rent, mortgage, electricity, water, etc."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:payroll skos:definition "The process of calculating and disbursing employee wages and salaries, including bonuses, health insurance, retirement contributions, etc."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:professional-and-contracted-services skos:definition
      "Expenses for services provided by external consultants or contractors, such as legal, accounting, consulting fees."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:recruiting-and-training skos:definition "Costs associated with attracting and developing employees."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:taxes-and-regulatory-fees skos:definition "Payments made to government entities, such as income tax, property tax, licensing fees, etc."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:travel-and-entertainment skos:definition "Expenses incurred for business-related travel and entertainment, such as employee travel, client entertainment."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:balance-sheet skos:definition "A snapshot of the organization's assets, liabilities and equity at a specific point in time."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:cash-flow skos:definition "A report that shows the movement of cash into and out of the organization over a period of time."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:changes-in-equity-statement skos:definition "A report that shows the changes in the organization's equity over a period of time."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:general-ledger skos:definition "A complete record of all financial transactions of the organization."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:income-statement skos:definition "A report that shows the organization's revenues, expenses and net income over a period of time."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:settlement-report skos:definition "A document that summarizes financial transactions between two parties."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:earnings-before-interest-taxes-depreciation-and-amortization
    skos:definition "An acronym for Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation and Amortization, a measure of the organization's operating profitability."@en .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-roadmap skos:definition "A high-level plan outlining the development timeline and key milestones for a product."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-vision-and-strategy skos:definition "Defining the overall direction and goals for a product or product line."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:portfolio-strategy skos:definition "A plan outlining how a company will manage its product portfolio to achieve its business objectives, including decisions about product development, pricing and product lifecycle management."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-catalog skos:definition "A comprehensive list of a company’s products or services, often with descriptions, pricing and other relevant information."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-features skos:definition "The characteristics and capabilities of a product, such as its size, weight, battery life and processing power."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:accessories skos:definition "Supplemental items that enhance the functionality or aesthetics of a core product, such as phone cases, screen protectors and headphones."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:connected-devices skos:definition "Devices that can connect to the internet or other devices, such as smartwatches, fitness trackers and home automation systems."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-premises-equipment skos:definition "Also known as CPE, equipment installed at a customer’s location to provide access to telecommunications services, such as modems, routers and set-top boxes."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:smartphone skos:definition "A mobile phone with advanced computing capabilities and connectivity features."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:audio-products skos:definition "Products related to sound devices, such as headphones, earphones, speakers and microphones."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:chargers-and-cables skos:definition "Power adapters and connecting cords used to charge electronic devices like smartphones, tablets and laptops."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:gaming-products skos:definition "Equipment and software designed for video games, including consoles, controllers and headsets."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:phone-attachments skos:definition "External devices that enhance smartphone functionality, including lenses, grips and portable projectors."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:phone-cases skos:definition "Protective covers for smartphones, offering impact resistance, scratch protection and personalized style."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:screen-protectors skos:definition "Thin films or tempered glass layers applied to smartphone and tablet screens to prevent scratches, cracks and smudges."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:smart-home-products skos:definition "Devices and systems that automate and control home functions, such as lighting, temperature, security and appliances."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:tablet-accessories skos:definition "Peripherals and add-ons for tablets, such as keyboards, styluses, cases and chargers."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:connected-home-devices skos:definition "Devices that connect to the internet and can be controlled remotely, such as smart thermostats, smart lighting and smart appliances."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:hum skos:definition "A device that plugs into a car’s OBD-II port and provides vehicle diagnostics, location tracking and other features."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:laptop skos:definition "A portable personal computer designed for mobile use."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:mobile-hotspot-devices skos:definition "Devices that create a Wi-Fi network using a cellular connection, allowing multiple devices to connect to the internet."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:security-cameras skos:definition "Cameras used for surveillance and security purposes."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:smartwatch skos:definition "A wearable device that functions as a watch and also provides smartphone-like functionality, such as notifications, fitness tracking and mobile payments."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:tablet skos:definition "A portable touchscreen device, larger than a smartphone but smaller than a laptop."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:routers skos:definition "Network devices that establish and manage internet connections, allowing multiple devices to share the same network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:set-top-boxes skos:definition "Devices that connect to televisions to provide access to cable or satellite TV channels, streaming services and other interactive features."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:universal-serial-bus-modems skos:definition "Devices that connect to a computer via USB and provide access to a cellular network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-compatibility skos:definition "Information about which other the organization products or services a specific product can successfully interact with or be used alongside."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-reviews-and-ratings skos:definition "Feedback and evaluations from customers who have purchased and used a product."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-warranty-and-support skos:definition "Guarantees and support services offered to customers who purchase a product."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network skos:definition "A group of interconnected devices that can communicate with each other."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-infrastructure skos:definition "The physical and logical components that support the operation of a computer network, including hardware, software and protocols."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-operations-center-management skos:definition
      "Overseeing and managing the operation and performance of a company’s network infrastructure."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:resource-catalog skos:definition "The process of acquiring, managing and disposing of assets effectively and efficiently."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:resource-investment skos:definition "Allocating financial and other resources to acquire, develop, or improve assets and capabilities."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-build skos:definition "The process of designing, deploying and configuring network infrastructure."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-capacity skos:definition "The maximum amount of data that a network can handle at a given time."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-configuration skos:definition "The settings and parameters that control the operation of a network and its devices."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-orchestration skos:definition "Automating the configuration, management and coordination of network resources and services."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-performance skos:definition "The speed, reliability and efficiency of a network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-specification skos:definition "A detailed description of the requirements and design of a network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-topology skos:definition "The physical or logical arrangement of devices and connections in a network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-utilization skos:definition "The amount of network capacity being used at a given time."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-network-performance skos:definition "The quality of network service experienced by end users."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:ethernet-backhaul-performance skos:definition "The performance of the Ethernet Backhaul (EBH), which affects the overall capacity and efficiency of the mobile network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:fixed-wireless-access-performance skos:definition "The performance of Fixed Wireless Access (FWA) connections, which affects the speed and reliability of internet access for customers."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-edge-performance skos:definition "The performance of edge computing resources, which affects the speed and latency of applications and services delivered to end users."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:radio-access-network-performance skos:definition "The performance of the Radio Access Network (RAN), which affects the speed and reliability of mobile data services."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:wireline-performance skos:definition "The overall quality and efficiency of a wired network, often measured by factors like speed, latency, uptime, and error rates."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:ethernet-backhaul-topology skos:definition "The arrangement of network elements in the Ethernet Backhaul (EBH)"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-edge-topology skos:definition "The arrangement of edge computing resources and connections."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:radio-access-network-topology skos:definition "The arrangement of cell towers, antennas and other components in the Radio Access Network (RAN)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:wireline-topology skos:definition "The physical and logical arrangement of cables, equipment, and connections within a wired network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:transport skos:definition "The movement of data across a network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:wireless-network skos:definition "A network that uses radio waves to transmit data, such as Wi-Fi and cellular networks."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:wireline-network skos:definition "A network that uses physical cables, such as copper wires or fiber optic cables, to transmit data."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:ethernet-backhaul skos:definition "Using wired Ethernet connections instead of wireless WiFi to transmit data between nodes in a mesh network or other distributed network setup. It provides a more stable and faster connection than Wi-Fi backhaul, ensuring a reliable data path between network devices."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:intelligent-edge-network skos:definition "A network architecture that distributes computing and networking resources closer to end users."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-edge skos:definition "The boundary between a company’s internal network and the internet or other external networks."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:radio-access-network skos:definition "RAN, the part of a telecommunications system that connects mobile devices to the core network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:backbone skos:definition "A high-speed, high-capacity network that forms the core of a larger network, connecting different parts of the network and providing a path for data to flow between them."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:big-rock-home-internet skos:definition "It provides internet service via a 5G or 4G LTE connection, serving as an alternative to traditional cable or fiber internet."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:private-mobile-radio skos:definition "A land-mobile radio service able to use radio frequencies assigned to a specific organization or entity for private voice and data communication."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-incident-response skos:definition "Responding to and resolving network incidents, such as outages, performance degradations and security breaches."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-monitoring skos:definition "Continuously tracking the status and performance of network devices and services to identify and resolve issues proactively."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-security skos:definition "Protecting network infrastructure and data from unauthorized access, use, disclosure, disruption, modification, or destruction."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:alarm skos:definition "A notification that indicates a potential problem or issue."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:extended-detection-and-response skos:definition "Extended Detection and Response, a security technology that provides comprehensive visibility and analysis of security threats across an organization’s entire IT infrastructure."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:issue-resolution skos:definition "The process of identifying, diagnosing and resolving network infrastructure issues."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:patch skos:definition "A software update that addresses vulnerabilities or bugs in a system."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:repair skos:definition "Fixing a physical or logical defect in a device or system."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:technician skos:definition "A skilled worker who installs, maintains and repairs technical equipment."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:test skos:definition "A procedure intended to establish the quality, performance, or reliability of something, especially before it is taken into widespread use."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:truck-roll skos:definition "Dispatching a technician to a customer’s location to resolve an issue."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:work-order skos:definition "A formal request for work to be performed, such as a repair or installation."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:ethernet-backhaul-fault-and-telemetry skos:definition
      "Alarms related to faults or performance issues in the Ethernet Backhaul (EBH)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:intelligent-edge-network-fault-and-telemetry skos:definition
      "Alarms related to faults or performance issues in edge computing infrastructure."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:radio-access-network-fault-and-telemetry skos:definition
      "Alarms related to faults or performance issues in the Radio Access Network (RAN)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:application skos:definition "A software program designed to perform specific tasks for users."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:asset skos:definition "A resource owned or controlled by a company that has economic value, such as property, equipment, or investments."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:carbon skos:definition "Carbon emissions, often used in the context of environmental sustainability and corporate social responsibility."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data skos:definition "Information processed or stored by a computer system."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:device skos:definition "An electronic gadget or appliance, such as a smartphone, tablet, or laptop."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:system skos:definition "A set of interconnected components that work together to achieve a common goal."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:mobile-application skos:definition "A software application designed to run on mobile devices, such as smartphones and tablets."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:ethernet-backhaul-asset skos:definition "Assets related to the Ethernet Backhaul (EBH)"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:fixed-wireless-access-asset skos:definition "Assets related to Fixed Wireless Access (FWA), which provides broadband internet access using wireless signals instead of traditional cable or DSL lines."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:intelligent-edge-network-asset skos:definition "Assets located at the edge of a network, closer to end users, such as edge computing servers and content delivery networks (CDNs)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:radio-access-network-asset skos:definition "Assets related to the Radio Access Network (RAN) in telecommunications, such as cell towers, antennas and base stations."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:connected-device skos:definition "A device that can connect to the internet or other devices, such as smartwatches, fitness trackers and home automation systems."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:mobile-device skos:definition "A portable electronic device, such as a smartphone or tablet."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:server skos:definition "A computer designed to process requests and deliver data to other computers over a network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:subscriber-identity-module-card skos:definition "A small card that stores subscriber information and allows a mobile device to connect to a cellular network."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:cost-per-acquisition skos:definition "Also known as CPA, the average cost of acquiring a new customer."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:total-cost-of-ownership skos:definition "Also known as TCO, the total cost of acquiring, owning and operating an asset over its entire lifecycle."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:integrated-service-management skos:definition "A holistic approach to managing all aspects of service delivery, from service design to customer support."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-activation skos:definition "The process of activating a new service for a customer."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-assurance skos:definition "Ensuring that services are delivered to customers at the agreed-upon quality and performance levels."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-availability skos:definition "The geographic areas where a service is offered and the quality of service available."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-catalog skos:definition "A structured repository that contains and organizes all network-related Service Specifications, including both abstract and resource-facing service definitions. It acts as the single source of truth for reusable, standard network service building blocks."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-cessation skos:definition "The process of discontinuing a service for a customer."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-configuration skos:definition "Setting up and customizing a service to meet a customer’s specific needs."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-level-agreement-management skos:definition
      "Defining, monitoring and reporting on service level agreements (SLAs) with customers."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-provisioning skos:definition "The process of creating and activating new services for customers, including setting up accounts, configuring services, and assigning resources."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-specification skos:definition "Defines the detailed technical and functional description of a network-facing service within the telecom operator’s infrastructure. It acts as a blueprint for creating consistent and reusable service instances that deliver specific network capabilities, independent of any customer or commercial context."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-usage skos:definition "The amount of a service that a customer uses during a billing cycle."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-change-management skos:definition "Managing changes to services to minimize disruptions and ensure a smooth transition."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-incident-management skos:definition "Responding to and resolving service interruptions or degradations."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-problem skos:definition "The underlying cause of one or more service incidents."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-problem-report skos:definition "A formal record of a service problem, including details about the issue and any steps taken to resolve it."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-problem-resolution skos:definition "The process of identifying and resolving the root cause of a service problem."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:feature-plans skos:definition "Service plans that offer specific features or benefits, such as unlimited texting or international calling."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-contract skos:definition "A formal agreement between a service provider and a customer that outlines the terms and conditions of service."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-plan skos:definition "A specific package of services offered at a particular price, such as a mobile phone plan or an internet plan."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:international-calling-and-travel skos:definition "Options for making and receiving calls and using data while traveling internationally."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:plan-compatibility skos:definition "Ensuring that a device is compatible with a particular service plan."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:plan-rate-and-access skos:definition "The pricing and terms of a service plan, including data allowances, speed limits and overage charges."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:connected-device-plans skos:definition "Service plans designed for connected devices, such as tablets, laptops and smartwatches."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:home-internet-plans skos:definition "Service plans designed for home internet access, typically offering different speeds and data allowances. Includes 5G Home Internet, LTE Home Internet, All Access Home Internet"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:smartphone-plans skos:definition "Service plans designed for smartphones, typically including voice calls, text messages and data."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-capacity skos:definition "The maximum workload, throughput, or number of concurrent users/transactions a service can handle while still meeting its defined performance targets and quality levels. It involves ensuring that the service has sufficient resources to meet current and future demand predictably."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-performance skos:definition "Measures how effectively a service is delivering on its promised quality and functionality from a user perspective. It encompasses various metrics like response time, availability, reliability, and throughput, ensuring the service meets agreed-upon service level objectives (SLOs)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:5g-availability skos:definition "The geographic areas where 5G cellular service is available."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:coverage-maps skos:definition "Maps that show the areas where a service provider offers coverage."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-outages skos:definition "Interruptions in service availability, often caused by technical issues or natural disasters."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:network-speed skos:definition "The speed at which data can be transmitted over a network, often measured in megabits per second (Mbps) or gigabits per second (Gbps)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:access-and-connectivity skos:definition "Services that provide access to communication networks and the internet."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:applications-and-value-added-services skos:definition
      "Services that provide additional functionality or value beyond basic access and connectivity."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:broadband-service skos:definition "High-speed internet access that provides a continuous connection to the internet."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:cloud-service skos:definition "Services delivered over the internet, such as data storage, computing power and software applications."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-usage skos:definition "The amount of data transmitted over a network, often measured in gigabytes (GB) or terabytes (TB)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:machine-to-machine skos:definition "Also known as M2M, Communication between devices without human intervention, often used in the Internet of Things (IoT)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:multimedia-messaging-service skos:definition "Also known as MMS, a service that allows users to send and receive multimedia messages, such as pictures, videos and audio files."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:number-porting skos:definition "Also called porting, the process of transferring a phone number from one service provider to another."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:pay-television skos:definition "Television services delivered through a paid subscription, such as cable TV and satellite TV."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:short-message-service skos:definition "Short Message Service (SMS), which allows users to send and receive text messages."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:voice-service skos:definition "Traditional telephone services that allow users to make and receive voice calls."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:business-digital-voice skos:definition "A cloud-based phone system designed for businesses, offering features like VoIP calling, voicemail-to-email, and virtual extensions."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:business-solutions skos:definition "Services designed to meet the specific needs of businesses, such as cloud computing, data analytics and customer relationship management (CRM) software."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:convenience-and-support skos:definition "Services that make life easier for customers, such as online bill pay, technical support and customer service."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:digital-entertainment-service skos:definition "Services that provide digital entertainment content, such as streaming music, movies and TV shows."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:family-and-safety skos:definition "Services designed to enhance family communication and safety, such as parental controls and location-based services."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:financial-services skos:definition "Services related to banking, investments and insurance."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:security-and-privacy skos:definition "Services designed to protect user data and privacy, such as antivirus software, firewalls and virtual private networks (VPNs)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:web-browsing skos:definition "Accessing and navigating websites on the internet."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:internet-protocol-television-service skos:definition
      "Internet Protocol Television (IPTV) service, which delivers television programming over the internet, such as YouTube TV."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:music-streaming-service skos:definition "A service that allows users to stream music over the internet, such as Spotify and Apple Music."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:vod-service skos:definition "Video on Demand (VOD) service, which allows users to watch movies and TV shows on demand, such as Netflix and Hulu."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:ehealth-service skos:definition "Electronic health services, such as telemedicine, remote patient monitoring and online health information."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:location-based-services skos:definition "Services that use a device’s location to provide relevant information or functionality, such as navigation apps and location-based advertising."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:early-termination-fees skos:definition "Fees charged to customers who cancel their service contract before the end of the agreed-upon term."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-level-agreement skos:definition "A formal agreement between a service provider and a customer that defines the level of service that will be provided."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-level-agreement-monitoring skos:definition
      "Tracking service performance against agreed-upon SLAs."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-level-agreement-reporting skos:definition "Providing regular reports to customers on service performance against SLAs."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:digital-subscriber-line-usage skos:definition "The amount of data transmitted over a Digital Subscriber Line (DSL) connection."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:calendar skos:definition "A system for organizing and scheduling events, appointments, and tasks for a party."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:communication-interaction skos:definition "An instance of communication or engagement between two or more parties."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:digital-identity skos:definition "The online presence and data associated with a party, which collectively represent that party in digital systems."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:location skos:definition "A physical or geographical place associated with a party, such as an address or a set of coordinates."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:party skos:definition "An individual, organization, or group that can enter into relationships or transactions."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:payment skos:definition "Information related to the financial transactions and payment methods associated with a party."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:privacy skos:definition "The right of a party to control the collection, use, and disclosure of their personal information."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:community skos:definition "A grouping of parties that share a common interest, characteristic, or relationship."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:contact-medium skos:definition "The method or channel through which communication or contact is made, such as email, phone, or social media."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:currency skos:definition "A system of money in general use in a particular country, represented as a unit of account and a medium of exchange."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:demographic skos:definition "Statistical data relating to a party, such as age, gender, income, or location, used for classification and analysis."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:identification skos:definition "A unique characteristic or credential that serves to establish the identity of a party."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:organization skos:definition "A type of party that is a legally recognized entity, such as a company, association, or government agency."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:permission skos:definition "The authorization granted to a party to perform a specific action or access certain information."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:profile skos:definition "A collection of data that provides a summary or overview of a particular party."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:role skos:definition "The function or capacity in which a party acts in a particular context or relationship."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:skill skos:definition "A specific ability or expertise possessed by a party."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:allowed-global-access skos:definition "Describes whether or not the Marketplace content is allowed to be viewed outside the United States."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:applicable-hub-and-spoke skos:definition "Describes the business spoke to which Marketplace content is related."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:billing-segment skos:definition "Describes the billing status of a customer's connection as relates to Marketplace content."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:care-channel skos:definition "Describes the customer care segments to which Marketplace content is related."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:categorization skos:definition "Information and digital assets must be classified according to the organization's information security needs, based on confidentiality, integrity, availability, and relevant interested party requirements."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-segment skos:definition "Describes the portion of the customer population to which Marketplace content is related."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:governance skos:definition "The holistic system of decision rights, policies, standards, and accountability frameworks that oversees how raw data is collected and managed, how semantic meaning and relationships are standardized, how analytical insights are derived, and how artificial intelligence models are developed and deployed—ensuring compliance, ethical alignment, operational trustworthiness, and business value across the entire intelligence lifecycle."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:metric-reporting-scope skos:definition "Indicates if the metric is reported internally within the organization, externally from the organization, or both."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:ownership skos:definition "The recognized right and practical capability to exercise exclusive control over a digital asset—including the powers to access, use, derive economic benefit from, restrict others from accessing, and irrevocably transfer or dispose of that asset—either through legal title (contractual and intellectual property rights) or cryptographic control (possession of private keys and ledger state authority)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:regulatory-classification skos:definition "Describes the Cybersecurity aligned specified data categories that assign classifications for Marketplace content based on applicable security controls and relevant regulations."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:sales-channel skos:definition "Describes the traditional the organization derived sales groupings to which Marketplace content is related."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:service-type skos:definition "Describes the traditional the organization business service areas to which Marketplace content is related."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-and-analytics-governance skos:definition "An acronym for Data and Analytics Governance."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:finance skos:definition "This spoke manages the organization's financial planning, reporting and analysis."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:human-resources skos:definition "An acronym for Human Resources, this spoke oversees employee-related matters such as hiring, training, benefits, and payroll."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:marketing-spoke skos:definition "This spoke develops and implements strategies to promote the organization's products and services."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:value skos:definition "This spoke is responsible for the wireless value brands."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:postpaid skos:definition "A billing model where the customer pays for services after usage, typically at the end of a billing cycle."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:prepaid skos:definition "A billing model where the customer pays for services before usage."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:calls skos:definition "Direct, real-time voice communication between a customer and a customer service representative."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:chat skos:definition "Real-time text-based communication between a customer and a customer service representative through a website or app."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:interactive-voice-response skos:definition "An acronym for Interactive Voice Response, this is a technology that allows customers to interact with a company’s phone system through voice prompts or keypad selections. This often involves navigating a menu to reach the appropriate department or information"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:retail skos:definition "Physical store locations where customers can interact with staff for assistance or information."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:social-media skos:definition "Using social media platforms as a channel for customers to reach out to a company for support or information."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:website skos:definition "A company’s online portal that may offer self-service resources like FAQs, knowledge bases and online forms for contacting support."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:marketplace-content-type skos:definition "Describes the type of Marketplace content."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:taxonomy-breadcrumb skos:definition "Inferred from assigned taxonomy node which shows the content hierarchy."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:dashboard skos:definition "Serves as an interactive data visualization interface to consolidate and display a combination of Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), metrics and critical data points on a single, easily digestible screen."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-product skos:definition "A curated and packaged dataset designed to deliver specific insights or solve a particular business problem."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:metrics skos:definition "A quantifiable measure used to track and evaluate the performance of a specific process, system, or objective. Metrics provide insights into key performance indicators (KPIs) and help businesses make data-driven decisions."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:model skos:definition "A mathematical representation of a process, system, or concept. In a marketplace, models are typically algorithms or statistical formulas trained on large datasets to make predictions, classifications, or generate insights. Examples include machine learning models for fraud detection or natural language processing models for sentiment analysis."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:report skos:definition "A structured presentation of data and information, often in a visual format, designed to communicate findings, insights, and recommendations. Reports can be static or interactive and are used to share analysis, track progress, or support decision-making."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:table skos:definition "A collection of data elements or datasets that make sense to group together, typically represented as a table."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:business skos:definition "Organizations that purchase goods or services to support their operations, production, or resale activities."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:consumer skos:definition "Individuals who purchase goods or services for personal use."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:enterprise-customer-segment skos:definition "Large-scale organizations, often with complex operations and a wide geographic reach."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:government skos:definition "Federal, state, or local government agencies that purchase goods and services for public use."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:medium-business skos:definition "Companies larger than small businesses but smaller than enterprises, with specific revenue and employee ranges depending on industry."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:multiple-dwelling-unit skos:definition "This is a building or complex comprising multiple separate residential units, such as apartments or condominiums."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:residential skos:definition "Relating to private homes and households."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:small-and-medium-sized-business skos:definition "This is Companies that fall below certain revenue or employee thresholds, varying by industry and country."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:wholesale skos:definition "The sale of goods in large quantities, typically to retailers, who then sell to consumers."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:certification-level skos:definition "Describes the current governance certification level of Marketplace content and is an important process within governance that can help establish controls that will enable accuracy and reliability."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:status skos:definition "A discrete, standardized state attribute that records an asset’s current condition, operational readiness, legal entitlement, or regulatory standing at a specific point within its cradle-to-grave continuum—serving as the formal trigger for governing transitions, access rights, accounting treatments, and maintenance actions"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:bronze skos:definition "A certification level that is used to gain understanding. This level establishes a baseline catalog with standard metadata attributes, establishes ownership and accountability, starts the data lineage journey & adopts intake and approval processes."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:gold skos:definition "A certification level that is used to establish trust. It enables automated controls and monitoring, monitors measurements and enables continuous improvement, establishes governance through full lifecycle from source & extends data lineage understanding to data source or origin."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:silver skos:definition "A certification level that is used to measure and monitor. This level establishes measurement of controls to determine effectiveness, establishes underlying data quality measurement framework & understands and documents classification from Legal and security point of view."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:uncertified skos:definition "Indicates that no certification level has been attained."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:active skos:definition "Currently in use or operation; fully functional and supported."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:deprecated skos:definition "No longer recommended for use and planned for retirement in the future; may have limited functionality or support."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:inactive skos:definition "Not currently in use but potentially reusable; may or may not be supported."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:retired skos:definition "Permanently out of use and not supported; typically kept for archival purposes."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:external skos:definition "Data and insights related to factors outside the organization’s direct control, such as market trends, competitor activity, or public perception. This data is often gathered from publicly available sources or third-party providers."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:internal skos:definition "Data and insights reflecting the performance, usage, or behavior within an organization’s own systems and processes. This data is typically not shared publicly."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:owner skos:definition "Describes the high-level owner of Marketplace content and to whom questions about Marketplace content can be directed."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:responsible-hub-and-spoke skos:definition "Describes which business spoke is ultimately responsible for the publication of Marketplace content."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:accountable-executive-sponsor skos:definition "An executive who is ultimately accountable for the metric. This person drives cross-domain coordination of strategies, provides an escalation path for the Metric Champion, and ensures data strategy is aligned to business strategy (typically a VP or above)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:business-process-owner skos:definition "The customer of data products. There could be more than one customer for a particular product – but there needs to be at least one."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:consulted-business-metric-stewards skos:definition
      "The Business Metric Stewards who represent the spokes who do not own this metric, but are to be consulted regarding it."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:consulted-spoke skos:definition "The spoke teams who represent the spokes who do not own this metric, but are to be consulted regarding it."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:consulted-technical-metric-stewards skos:definition
      "The Technical Metric Stewards who represent the spokes who do not own this metric, but are to be consulted regarding it."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-architect skos:definition "Ensures solution aligns with overall technical vision, product architecture fits together."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-product-analyst skos:definition "Data products must have this role which develops analysis and provide technical product requirements as needed. They deeply understand the data, its use-cases and its business context."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-product-governance skos:definition "Ensures product is not redundant, confirms compliance with governance standards, certifies product"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-product-owner skos:definition "Data products must have this role which provides solutions to the needs of business process owners. They are the single point of contact for the business process owner. They are accountable for establishing the overall feature roadmap, including the prioritization and initial feature sequencing, for understanding the technical challenges necessary for developing that roadmap, ensuring the product meets their customers’ needs, identifying new use cases for the product, etc."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:data-scientist skos:definition "Data products may have this role which develops reusable production ML models. They’re responsible for model creation, model performance, and model refresh/rebuild."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:machine-learning-engineer skos:definition "Data products may have this role which develops production ML model scoring pipelines. They’re responsible for scoring pipeline, model API, and model monitoring."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:product-group-coordinator skos:definition "Scrum-master-in-chief; same role as a scrum master, for a group of products. Does not interact with customers or translate business needs."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:responsible-business-metric-stewards skos:definition
      "This role fully understands the business context of the metric and very often comes up with the need for the metric, defines and manages the business definition, objectives and purpose of the metric, provides business formula for the calculation of the metric in simple understandable language, manages & approves all business decisions related to the metric, and is responsible for ongoing maintenance of business metadata of the metric."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:responsible-business-report-stewards skos:definition
      "This role fully understands the business context of the report and very often comes up with the need for the report, defines and manages the business definition, objectives and purpose of the report, manages & approves all business decisions related to the report, and is responsible for ongoing maintenance of business metadata of the report."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:responsible-metric-champion skos:definition "A leader who is responsible for the overall strategy regarding the metric (typically a Sr. Director or above)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:responsible-technical-metric-stewards skos:definition
      "This role not only understands the business context, objectives and purpose of the metric, but is also responsible for defining the technical details of metric calculations. This individual is responsible for understanding and defining one or many of the following details: how a metric should be calculated, which are the best data sources for pulling the data for calculations, what additional calculations need to be made in order to report the metric (Report/Dashboard etc.). This person approves all decisions that affect the data used in calculating a metric."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:responsible-technical-report-stewards skos:definition
      "This role not only understands the business context, objectives and purpose of the report, but is also responsible for defining the technical details of the report. This individual is responsible for understanding and defining many report details."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:scrum-master skos:definition "Data products may have this role which enables a team's delivery across sprints. They manage sprint planning/iteration, facilitate daily standups, administrate the team's board, and capture retrospective opportunities."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:solution-leader skos:definition "Data products must have this role which is the delivery owner for the data product. They define the product's technical vision and own the in-depth delivery of the product's technical solution and are responsible for the product's technical performance. They confirm that the correct skills are present for technical delivery, and work to resolve gaps."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:controlled-unclassified-information skos:definition
      "An acronym for Controlled Unclassified Information is a category of federal ”unclassified information” the USG creates or processes, or that an entity creates or possesses for, or on behalf of, the US Government that requires safeguarding and dissemination protections. 1 the organization (the organization) CUI information examples include: Export Control, Systems Vulnerability, Technical Configurations, Controlled Technical Information"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:critical-infrastructure-information skos:definition
      "An abbreviation for Critical Infrastructure Information, this is data pertaining to U.S. critical infrastructure services provided by the organization."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:customer-proprietary-network-information skos:definition
      "An acronym for Customer Proprietary Network Information, generally considered a subset or subcategory of PII"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:employee-information skos:definition "An abbreviation for Employee Information, this is records associated with employees (past or present) of the organization and is generally considered a subset or subcategory of PII. May also be called personnel information (PERS)."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:export-controlled-information skos:definition "An abbreviation for Export Controlled Information, this is data subject to various export controls"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:global-sensitive-account-management skos:definition
      "An acronym for Global Sensitive Account Management Information, this is data associated with GSAM designated customer identities"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:payment-card-industry skos:definition "An acronym for Payment Card Industry, this is data related to credit and debit card holders."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:personally-identifiable-information skos:definition
      "An acronym for Personally Identifiable Information, any representation of information that permits the identity of an individual to whom the information applies to be reasonably inferred by either direct or indirect means."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:protected-health-information skos:definition "An acronym for Protected Health Information, this information is generally considered a subset or subcategory of PII"@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:sarbanes-oxley skos:definition "An acronym for Sarbanes-Oxley 404, this is information related to compliance with the control."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:field skos:definition "A sales channel involving sales representatives who travel to meet with potential customers in person, often at their place of business or events."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:in-house skos:definition "A sales channel where employees of the company directly sell products or services to customers, typically through phone, email, or online chat."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:indirect skos:definition "A sales channel that relies on intermediaries, such as distributors, resellers, or affiliates, to sell products or services on behalf of the company."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:retail-sales skos:definition "A sales channel where products are sold directly to consumers through physical stores owned or operated by the company."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:system-integrator skos:definition "An acronym for System Integrator, this is a specialized type of indirect partner that designs, builds, and implements complex technology systems, often incorporating products or services from multiple vendors."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:telesales skos:definition "A sales channel where sales representatives contact potential customers over the phone to generate leads, qualify prospects, or close deals."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:value-added-reseller skos:definition "An acronym for Value-Added Reseller, this is a type of indirect channel partner that not only sells a company’s products but also adds value by providing additional services, such as customization, integration, or support."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
  applicationbusinesstaxonomyvoc:wireless skos:definition "Also known in business use as Mobile, this is a service type that uses radio waves to transmit and receive data, offering mobility and flexibility without physical connections."@en;
    skos:inScheme <https://www.insperity.com/vocabulary/application-business-taxonomy/> .
  
